<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan sugar imports down 26.5 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan sugar imports down 26.5 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian imports of all types of sugar fell 26.5 percent to 90,800 tonnes in January from the previous month, State Customs Committee figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The committee, quoted by Interfax news agency, put December 1996 total sugar imports at 123,500 tonnes.</p>
<p>It gave no comparative breakdowns for raws and whites but said January refined sugar imports were 60,800 tonnes.</p>
<p>January sugar shipments from Ukraine were 46,800 tonnes, while deliveries from Brazil were 29,200 tonnes, it said.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
